WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.699 --> 00:00:04.650
Elon Musk used to own plenty of real estate
in California.

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.519
But in 2020 he went on a huge selling spree,
parting ways with his multi-million dollar

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:13.480
properties one by one by one by one.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.820
In total, he’s sold seven houses.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.440
His eighth and only remaining home - a beautiful,
Bay area estate that he describes as a special

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.210
place - hit the market in June.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.600
The price: $37.5 million.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.780
Not long ago, Musk packed his bags and moved
to Texas - which, by the way, has no personal

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.010
income tax.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:35.470
Whereas the Golden State imposes the highest
level of income tax on its richest residents.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:38.750
There are plenty of fancy homes in
south Texas a half hours’ drive from Boca

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:42.020
Chica where SpaceX built its rocket facility
for Starship.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:46.300
But the second richest person in the world
says instead, he’s chosen to rent a small

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:52.240
home from his company located by the production
site worth a mere $50,000.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.030
He reportedly lives in a foldable house in
a box like this according to Teslarati.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:02.200
The windows and walls unfold into a 400-square
foot space complete with a kitchen, bathroom,

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.520
bedroom, and living room.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.729
They’re built by a startup called Boxabl
which had no comment about Musk’s living

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:09.389
situation when I reached out to them.

00:01:09.389 --> 00:01:12.920
But the company has certainly been dropping
hints about a new customer.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:17.799
In a promotional video from late 2020, Boxabl
showed off one of its units with a photo of

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:21.509
SpaceX’s Falcon 9 and had this
to say about a special delivery.

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:26.189
We just installed in Boca Chica, Texas for
a top-secret customer.

00:01:26.189 --> 00:01:27.189
Pretty exciting to have these guys of our
initial customer.

00:01:27.189 --> 00:01:32.490
The portable homes have a starting price of
$49,500 and are light enough to be towed by

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.609
a Model X which costs twice
as much.

00:01:35.609 --> 00:01:40.310
By living on-site - Musk has 24/7 access to all of SpaceX’s developments as

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:44.459
it powers full steam ahead in the hopes of
sending humans to Mars.

00:01:44.459 --> 00:01:48.109
Musk has famously signaled his commitment
to his companies by placing himself right

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:49.369
in the center of the action.

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:53.969
Like the times he sleeps at Tesla’s factories
which I talked about in another video.

00:01:53.969 --> 00:01:57.829
Or further back, when he and his brother started
their first company, he slept at the office

00:01:57.829 --> 00:01:59.899
and showered at the YMCA.

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:04.549
In this case - his vision of a factory line
of fully reusable launch vehicles supersedes

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:07.579
any desire for luxurious living.

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:12.160
Downsizing his house is a metaphor for downsizing
his life in order to focus on his ambitions.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.880
And if making life multi-planetary weren’t
enough, he’s trying to solve traffic congestion

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.200
with the Boring Company, wants to make humans
smarter by implanting tiny wires with Neuralink,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.540
and then of course there’s his electric
car company Tesla which has a Gigafactory

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.780
under construction in Austin.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.629
His girlfriend Grimes confirmed she has also moved
to the Texas capital.

00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:33.840
Musk is not the only billionaire to live frugally.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.480
Facebook’s Mark Zuckerberg famously has
a wardrobe of simple, gray shirts.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.409
One of the most successful investors of all time, Warren Buffet, often eats breakfast

00:02:42.409 --> 00:02:43.409
at McDonald’s.

00:02:43.409 --> 00:02:49.532
And still lives in the same house in Omaha
that he purchased in 1958 for $31,500.

00:02:49.532 --> 00:02:53.120
Still, it’s nothing like a tiny home in
a box.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.489
Musk has also been seen at another property
in Boca Chica village right next to SpaceX’s site.

00:02:58.489 --> 00:03:02.819
The CEO has been spotted staying at this house
that SpaceX remodeled and is said to be one

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:04.310
of the nicest in the neighborhood.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:09.800
It was appraised at $47,000 in 2020 and is
now worth more than three times that according

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.379
to the Wall Street Journal.

00:03:11.379 --> 00:03:15.200
Real estate in Boca Chica has soared in value
since Musk appealed for people to move to

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:20.000
the area and said SpaceX would have thousands of job openings in the next few years.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.879
Boca Chica is a tiny community.

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:26.840
There are only about 40 houses here with no shops, restaurants, or even water pipes.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.079
Water is trucked in.

00:03:28.079 --> 00:03:31.890
The people who live here are mostly retired
and come to spend the winters.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:34.200
SpaceX has been offering to buy all the houses.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.680
Some residents have taken the money while
others have refused and have complained of

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.769
bullying by SpaceX to try and get them to
sell.

00:03:40.769 --> 00:03:44.689
South Texas is precious to SpaceX because
of its proximity to the equator which gives

00:03:44.689 --> 00:03:47.810
rockets a boost in speed due to the rotation
of the Earth.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.659
The company also has a long history in the
Lonestar state.

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:54.799
It’s had a rocket engine testing site north
of Austin for two decades.

00:03:54.799 --> 00:03:58.879
SpaceX has hinted that it wants to develop
the Boca Chica area into a resort.

00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:02.519
It posted a job for a resort development manager
in 2020.

00:04:02.519 --> 00:04:06.159
Musk envisions a city called Starbase that
would incorporate the small community.

00:04:06.159 --> 00:04:10.890
Boxabl has even pitched the idea of
more housing units for the expansion of Starbase.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.099
As for this $50,000 humble abode?

00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:17.100
Musk is unlikely to buy million-dollar digs
in the future.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.750
He has said his plan is to not own a home.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.540
Who needs one  when Mars is calling?

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:25.200
To call Musk a busy man is an understatement.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:30.439
He reportedly plans his day in five-minute
slots in order to make the best use of his time.

00:04:30.439 --> 00:04:34.350
